# What EAS does NOT need to upload.
#
# This file REPLACES .gitignore when EAS packs the project, so it has to repeat
# the build output as well as name the extra things. The patterns are
# deliberately unanchored — they match at any depth — because the archive is
# taken at the workspace root while this file sits beside eas.json.

# Dependencies and build output
node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
.expo/
DerivedData/
build/

# The two GENERATED native projects, spelled with their parent directory.
#
# A bare `ios/` looks right and is wrong: these patterns match at any depth, so
# it also swallows `modules/hermie-mac/ios/`, and an archive missing that builds
# an app whose local Expo module simply is not there. `npx expo-doctor` fails on
# it, which is how this was found. Naming the parent cannot match anything under
# `modules/`, and if the archive root ever changes the only cost is uploading a
# directory EAS regenerates anyway.
hermie/ios/
hermie/android/

# Documentation, design sources and screenshots
docs/
design/
*.md

# Local state
*.log
.env
.env.local
.DS_Store
